"""The L2 compiler: parser, compile-time VM, x86-64 emitter, CLI and daemon.

It is one file on purpose: it is easy to copy, and splitting it would not
make startup faster.  Heavy standard-library modules load lazily.  Sections
are marked `# § N. Title`; search for "§ N." to jump to one.

  §  1. Startup: lazy modules, keystone
  §  2. Events: subscriptions, EventBus, JSON projection
  §  3. Diagnostics and compiler errors
  §  4. Source origins, expansion frames, quotations, match specs
  §  5. Tokenizer (Reader, raw :asm bodies)
  §  6. IR ops, words, peephole tables
  §  7. Rewrites
  §  8. Token hooks and language packs
  §  9. Dictionary and definition candidates
  § 10. Parser
  § 11. Compile-time VM
  § 12. NASM emitter helpers
  § 13. CT native equivalents of stdlib :asm words
  § 14. Assembler: emission and optimization
  § 15. Built-in macros and compile-time words
  § 16. Runtime intrinsics for --ct-run-main
  § 17. Bootstrap dictionary (registers every CT word)
  § 18. Driver: source units, imports, Compiler, caches, toolchain
  § 19. REPL
  § 20. Integrity checks (--check-integrity)
  § 21. Warm stdlib (daemon workers)
  § 22. Command-line interface
  § 23. Compile daemon
  § 24. Entry point
"""

